{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 50, :comments ["<b>And die on the mountain.</b> The sage Rabbi Abraham, of blessed memory, explained the form ומות — 'and die' — as meaning that he should prepare himself thereby, for he buried himself. And it is possible to interpret the sense of ומות — 'and die' — as: I decree upon you that you shall die immediately; for death is not in man's hand, and therefore you will not find in the language of the Holy Tongue a word in the imperative mode for a thing that man has no power to do immediately, such as sleep and death — for one speaking with his fellow cannot say to him ישן ('sleep!') or מות ('die!'), since it is impossible for him to sleep or to die at once. But since Scripture here says ומות, it is the word of HaShem — and He, may He be exalted, is the One who decrees, and His is the dominion and the power."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:38.541689585Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}